The dogfood paragraph of docs/features/cli-and-mcp.md now says:
- a slow call whose record has not arrived prints 'unavailable (record not yet received)' at once, then its record when it arrives;
- a record that never comes reads unavailable at close;
- an evicted, incomplete or cancelled record reads 'unavailable (record STATE)' with its fields.
Gate 9/9, the pair was clean, and the evaluation passed. Landed as 242249f and installed as build 5f72edbf.
